WEBVTT


00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:24.494
- El Presidente.
- Mm-hm.


00:01:42.252 --> 00:01:43.549
Ah-ah.


00:02:01.471 --> 00:02:03.200
Turn around, yeah.


00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.339
Move up right, get behind that wall.
It's good cover.


00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.073
Get down, get down.
Move to the right.


00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:20.120
Nice shooting, 91.


00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.349
Like the way I look holding a gun,
baby girl?


00:02:22.525 --> 00:02:25.585
Don't call me that, I was being sarcastic.
You didn't hit anything.


00:02:25.762 --> 00:02:27.992
So what? At least I look good.


00:02:28.164 --> 00:02:30.826
When there's real bad guys,
you get your head blown off...


00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.093
...at least your arms
will still look awesome.


00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:36.466
- Look, the boys need to breathe.
- Mm-hm.


00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:40.167
You and the boys go left,
and I'll come in behind.


00:02:40.343 --> 00:02:42.311
I got a little something else
up my sleeve.


00:02:42.478 --> 00:02:45.572
- Not that this isn't plenty.
- Ugh...


00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:48.911
Come on, we don't have time for this.
What is it?


00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.315
Watch this.


00:02:53.623 --> 00:02:54.783
Whoa.


00:02:55.291 --> 00:02:57.259
Optical Camouflage Technology.


00:02:57.427 --> 00:03:00.225
A little something Bruce and Lloyd
been working on for me.


00:03:00.396 --> 00:03:03.559
So you go left,
and I'll sneak in behind them.


00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:04.757
Good luck, baby girl.


00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.300
Warriors, come out and play.


00:03:11.507 --> 00:03:13.873
Yoo-hoo! Ha-ha-ha.


00:03:14.043 --> 00:03:16.568
Hey, what rhymes with CIA?


00:03:16.746 --> 00:03:18.145
Loser.


00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.380
Hold your fire, hold your fire.


00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:24.850
That's a dummy, dummies.


00:03:25.021 --> 00:03:27.046
With my clothes.


00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.620
Why do they call you the CIA anyway?
They should call you the DAS.


00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:32.818
Dumb as shit.


00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.454
And ugly too. Get out of my face.


00:03:35.865 --> 00:03:37.389
Whoa. Hey, what was that for?


00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.028
Take that.
- Take that, take that.


00:03:40.203 --> 00:03:41.465
- Ow! My balls.
- Oh, my...


00:03:41.938 --> 00:03:42.962
Wait a minute, stop.


00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:46.870
That's beautiful.
Time for an invisible victory dance.


00:03:47.911 --> 00:03:50.573
I guess CONTROL kicked your ass.


00:03:51.047 --> 00:03:52.878
<i>We beat you, we beat you, that's right.</i>


00:03:53.049 --> 00:03:57.179
<i>That's for you, that's for you.
You lose, we win, we win.</i>


00:03:57.353 --> 00:04:00.811
<i>You lose and spin it
and spin it and spin it. Let's go.</i>


00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.989
What are you doing?


00:04:06.696 --> 00:04:07.924
I thought I was invisible.


00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:10.663
Even if you were, what are you doing?


00:04:13.403 --> 00:04:15.564
Hey, come on, fellas. It's all in fun.


00:04:15.738 --> 00:04:17.103
You guys are like family.


00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:20.533
<i>I'm sorry. Hey, hey, I'm sorry.</i>


00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.734
Battery life.


00:04:21.911 --> 00:04:24.345
It's a limiting factor
in so many technologies.


00:04:24.514 --> 00:04:26.209
<i>- My eye.
So frustrating.</i>


00:04:26.582 --> 00:04:27.844
Can you mute that?


00:04:28.017 --> 00:04:29.678
<i>- Sweet mother of God.
- Yeah.</i>


00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:31.547
Thanks.


00:04:34.824 --> 00:04:37.349
They're close to perfecting the OCT.
We should move.


00:04:37.794 --> 00:04:39.318
Good work.


00:04:39.762 --> 00:04:41.127
We're on.


00:04:41.297 --> 00:04:43.265
Americans spying on Americans.


00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:44.695
Somehow that seems so...


00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:46.027
Patriotic?


00:04:46.202 --> 00:04:47.328
Exactly.


00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.035
Hey, did you hear
Max didn't make agent?


00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.271
Sorry about that.
- No problem.


00:04:56.446 --> 00:04:59.574
He took the test and everything,
but the chief wouldn't promote him.


00:04:59.749 --> 00:05:02.843
He's a great analyst.
I say be happy with what you're good at.


00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:05.749
Look at us. We're good
at tech stuff, so that's what we do.


00:05:05.922 --> 00:05:08.254
- Best weapons money can buy.
- Bruce.


00:05:08.424 --> 00:05:10.585
Total dedication.


00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.251
- Man, I'm hungry, early lunch?
- Definitely.


00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.598
I will fix this.


00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:54.831
Why is that door always broken?


00:05:55.004 --> 00:05:57.302
Why is our main elevator
a telephone booth?


00:05:57.473 --> 00:05:58.997
Good point.


00:06:00.209 --> 00:06:03.201
Oh, hello, underchief.
- Where are you two going, early lunch?


00:06:03.379 --> 00:06:04.539
- Yes. Why?
- No. Why?


00:06:04.714 --> 00:06:07.376
Good Lord, we're in the spy business.
Lie better.


00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.677
I was over at the Pentagon
getting an earful...


00:06:09.852 --> 00:06:13.083
...about when they're gonna see
your Optical Camouflage Technology.


00:06:13.256 --> 00:06:14.518
Well, they'll never see it.


00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:15.714
It's invisible.


00:06:18.828 --> 00:06:21.160
Uh, sir, we did test
the OCT this morning...


00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.730
...and we're still having
a tiny battery-life issue.


00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.391
But I am sure
we'll easily make our delivery date.


00:06:26.569 --> 00:06:28.764
Which has been moved up
to the end of this week.


00:06:28.938 --> 00:06:31.372
- When did that happen?
- Just now, didn't you hear me?


00:06:31.541 --> 00:06:35.534
My arrogant brother at the CIA would love
to see me fail, and that's not gonna happen.


00:06:35.711 --> 00:06:39.306
Not when I'm next in line to be top dog,
should our beloved chief ever retire.


00:06:39.482 --> 00:06:42.474
- I mean, what is he, 200?
- Well, he uses a lot of moisturizer.


00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:44.847
We're done talking here. Make a hole.


00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:47.981
Think I'll give my brother a call.


00:06:48.157 --> 00:06:51.092
See if I can't make
that little vein in his eye pop again.


00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:58.900
Not one word.


00:07:01.104 --> 00:07:02.264
<i>Hello?</i>


00:07:02.438 --> 00:07:04.133
<i>Hello? Who's there?</i>


00:07:04.307 --> 00:07:06.673
It's me, I'll call you back.


00:07:07.443 --> 00:07:09.707
The OCT's our most important project.


00:07:09.879 --> 00:07:12.074
We can't let
it be another failed experiment.


00:07:12.248 --> 00:07:13.340
It's not failed.


00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:15.916
It just doesn't work. Ah.


00:07:16.085 --> 00:07:19.646
No worse than your, uh, super stun gun.
Makes people laugh.


00:07:19.822 --> 00:07:21.084
Maybe I wanted it that way.


00:07:21.257 --> 00:07:22.952
Oh, Tickle Taser? Giggle Gun?


00:07:23.126 --> 00:07:25.458
Yeah, your crappy little peashooter
is any better?


00:07:25.628 --> 00:07:27.596
It's supposed
to be a crowd-control weapon.


00:07:27.763 --> 00:07:30.231
You know, high-energy beam
makes you fall unconscious.


00:07:30.399 --> 00:07:34.358
Unfortunately, all it does is this.


00:07:42.645 --> 00:07:45.307
Oh, it looks like the underchief.
Just with more hair.


00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.144
What?


00:07:53.456 --> 00:07:54.787
You staring at my hair?


00:07:54.957 --> 00:07:57.983
I know, I know,
my girlfriend put in these highlights.


00:07:58.928 --> 00:08:01.761
That's it, I'm gonna wash them out.
They look ridiculous.


00:08:02.832 --> 00:08:05.164
- He's gonna lose the rest of his hair?
- Oh, yeah.


00:08:05.334 --> 00:08:07.393
In three, two, one.


00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.594
Oh, my God.


00:08:08.771 --> 00:08:09.795
Oh, my God.


00:08:09.972 --> 00:08:11.064
Oh, my God.


00:08:15.178 --> 00:08:18.147
- Hey, Nina, how's the forensics lab?
- Oh, it's pretty bad.


00:08:18.314 --> 00:08:20.646
I lost almost
all my flesh-eating beetle larvae.


00:08:20.816 --> 00:08:22.113
- Oh, bummer.
- Yeah.


00:08:26.756 --> 00:08:28.280
Nina.


00:08:29.859 --> 00:08:31.258
Oh, is that her name?


00:08:31.894 --> 00:08:33.259
I didn't know that.


00:08:33.429 --> 00:08:34.453
Yeah, right.


00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.097
You totally like her.


00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:38.199
- She smells funny.
- So what? She's hot.


00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:41.825
She's pretty, but she works with dead flesh.
That smell doesn't dissipate.


00:08:42.405 --> 00:08:44.066
No, he actually said that?


00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.401
Oh, no, that is so wrong.


00:08:46.576 --> 00:08:49.511
You know what?
If you ask me, I think I...


00:08:49.745 --> 00:08:51.235
Mm.


00:08:51.547 --> 00:08:53.674
I'm gonna call you back on a landline.


00:08:54.517 --> 00:08:57.077
Fine. Come on, Mr. Picky,
we got work to do.


00:08:57.253 --> 00:08:58.345
Okay.


00:09:02.592 --> 00:09:05.755
The power matrix for the OCT
only lasts for about six minutes.


00:09:05.928 --> 00:09:08.829
That's disgusting.
They put cheese on a pretzel?


00:09:08.998 --> 00:09:10.727
Oh, you can put cheese on anything.


00:09:17.673 --> 00:09:18.799
Holy Lord.


00:09:18.975 --> 00:09:20.306
Dude, you said that really...


00:09:20.476 --> 00:09:21.704
Holy Lord.


00:09:21.877 --> 00:09:24.141
- Static electricity is the answer.
- Yes, it is.


00:09:24.313 --> 00:09:27.646
No, the battery-life problem to the OCT.


00:09:27.817 --> 00:09:31.719
The fabric is very staticky, which
we thought was a problem, but what if?


00:09:31.887 --> 00:09:35.084
What if we added another fiber
to create positive and negative poles?


00:09:35.258 --> 00:09:37.726
Allowing the motion of fabric
to generate electricity.


00:09:37.893 --> 00:09:40.453
Then it could recharge its own batteries.
That's genius.


00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.654
No.


00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:45.494
Genius would be to follow her
to see if the static increases or decreases.


00:09:45.668 --> 00:09:47.363
Oh, I agree.


00:09:51.507 --> 00:09:53.270
Here we go.


00:09:53.442 --> 00:09:55.273
Check it out.


00:09:55.444 --> 00:09:59.244
We've just boosted the charge to last
about 24 hours, thank you very much.


00:09:59.415 --> 00:10:01.042
That is excellent.


00:10:01.217 --> 00:10:04.846
- We're back in the win column, my friend.
- You know, I feel proud.


00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:07.080
Already we're rising from the ashes.


00:10:07.256 --> 00:10:09.781
This technology's
gonna do some real good in the world.


00:10:09.959 --> 00:10:11.483
And you know what that means.


00:10:11.661 --> 00:10:14.721
Yes, you can lower your goofy hands
and do something useful.


00:10:14.897 --> 00:10:16.057
Let's order the keg.


00:10:28.077 --> 00:10:29.237
Don't drink and drive.


00:10:30.112 --> 00:10:32.046
This may be our finest hour.


00:10:32.214 --> 00:10:34.739
I know. I just wish Max were here.


00:10:38.921 --> 00:10:40.855
Tickle Taser.


00:10:42.258 --> 00:10:45.056
I'm glad somebody's getting
some use out of that thing.


00:10:45.227 --> 00:10:47.821
This is the coolest thing ever.
How does it work?


00:10:47.997 --> 00:10:50.022
Turns any pair of shoes into gecko feet.


00:10:50.199 --> 00:10:52.565
Unbelievable, you guys are geniuses.


00:10:52.735 --> 00:10:57.172
Hey, hey, hand me a margarita. I'm gonna
try and drink it while... Whoa! Oh...


00:10:58.074 --> 00:10:59.564
Well, that explains it.


00:10:59.742 --> 00:11:01.403
He didn't double knot.


00:11:07.383 --> 00:11:08.782
Who's that talking to Neil?


00:11:08.951 --> 00:11:10.111
She seems nice.


00:11:10.519 --> 00:11:13.488
- How do you know she's nice?
- She's talking to Neil.


00:11:13.656 --> 00:11:15.146
He doesn't even have eyebrows.


00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:23.330
Hi, Lloyd.
What do you want to do with me?


00:11:26.635 --> 00:11:28.193
I win again.


00:11:28.371 --> 00:11:31.465
Darn, I've gotten so bad at this game.


00:11:33.542 --> 00:11:34.873
Lloyd, Bruce.


00:11:35.044 --> 00:11:36.636
Bob Mansfield, CIA.


00:11:36.812 --> 00:11:38.507
Yes, Bob, we've met.


00:11:38.681 --> 00:11:40.410
Many times.


00:11:41.083 --> 00:11:43.278
<i>Hola, amigos, sweet fiesta.</i>


00:11:43.452 --> 00:11:46.148
Word around the CIA
is you've perfected the battery life...


00:11:46.322 --> 00:11:48.187
...of the Optical Camouflage Technology.


00:11:48.357 --> 00:11:50.848
- How'd you know about that?
- Um, we're the CIA.


00:11:51.026 --> 00:11:54.462
- Gonna give us a peek, a little looksie-loo?
- We're not showing it to you.


00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.326
You're just gonna reverse engineer
and take all the credit.


00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:01.095
Besides, sharing has to go both ways.
Otherwise, it's called taking.


00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:03.534
Like what you did with my Wii controller.


00:12:03.706 --> 00:12:06.140
- Thought I gave that back.
- No, you didn't.


00:12:06.308 --> 00:12:09.334
Hey, Nina. Hey, how's it going?
You having a good time?


00:12:09.512 --> 00:12:11.639
- Yeah, it's great.
- Bruce, it's Nina.


00:12:11.814 --> 00:12:13.748
- Check it out, Nina.
- Hey, hi.


00:12:13.916 --> 00:12:15.281
How's things at Forensics?


00:12:15.451 --> 00:12:17.180
Mm, pretty dead, actually.


00:12:19.321 --> 00:12:20.754
- It's awesome.
- Ha-ha-ha.


00:12:20.923 --> 00:12:23.016
Nobody in my family ever gets that joke.


00:12:23.192 --> 00:12:24.216
I totally got it.


00:12:24.393 --> 00:12:26.088
I got it too. Ha-ha-ha.


00:12:28.798 --> 00:12:30.629
All right, well, see you.


00:12:32.101 --> 00:12:33.125
That was weird.


00:12:33.302 --> 00:12:34.360
She didn't smell funny.


00:12:34.537 --> 00:12:36.869
Yeah, I noticed that too.


00:12:37.039 --> 00:12:39.906
- Maybe you should talk to her a bit more.
- Nah. Not the right time.


00:12:40.075 --> 00:12:42.043
No, I think you should do it right now.


00:12:42.211 --> 00:12:44.679
- Do it, do it, do it.
- Gotta go slowly, let it simmer.


00:12:44.847 --> 00:12:46.974
Low probability of success,
makes me desperate.


00:12:47.149 --> 00:12:49.379
Hey, you're already desperate.
Go get her.


00:12:51.987 --> 00:12:53.477
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:12:53.656 --> 00:12:55.055
May I offer you a refill?


00:12:55.224 --> 00:12:56.589
Yeah, sure. Thank you.


00:12:59.795 --> 00:13:03.492
- Um... Sorry, looks like the keg is out.
- Oh.


00:13:04.133 --> 00:13:05.395
Um...


00:13:06.769 --> 00:13:08.737
Well, I've got some alcohol up in the lab.


00:13:08.904 --> 00:13:10.929
Yeah, but that's isopropyl alcohol.


00:13:11.106 --> 00:13:13.870
It's just disinfectant.
If you drink it, it'll kill you.


00:13:14.043 --> 00:13:17.274
I was actually talking about
the bottle of tequila in my desk. Ha.


00:13:19.315 --> 00:13:22.842
I work with dead bodies.
Sometimes I need to unwind. Ahem.


00:13:23.018 --> 00:13:24.417
Let's unwind.


00:13:24.587 --> 00:13:26.487
Okay.


00:13:32.161 --> 00:13:33.924
Hello, I'm Isabella.


00:13:34.363 --> 00:13:36.524
Hello, Is...


00:13:42.771 --> 00:13:44.568
Okay.


00:13:48.544 --> 00:13:50.205
Dang it.


00:13:57.353 --> 00:13:58.684
Great party last night.


00:13:58.854 --> 00:14:00.412
Way better than last year's.


00:14:00.589 --> 00:14:01.613
Well, yeah.


00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:03.417
No one vomited in the centrifuge.


00:14:03.592 --> 00:14:06.152
Yeah, that was a lot of paper towels.


00:14:10.633 --> 00:14:12.191
- What was that?
- I don't know.


00:14:12.368 --> 00:14:14.029
Come on, help me with the door.


00:14:25.047 --> 00:14:26.446
Oh, man.


00:14:35.824 --> 00:14:37.951
We're gonna die.


00:14:38.127 --> 00:14:39.355
Wait a minute.


00:14:39.528 --> 00:14:42.986
Why is my life not flashing
before my eyes?


00:14:43.165 --> 00:14:44.325
Your mother's right.


00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.525
Oh, my God, I do have no life.


00:14:46.702 --> 00:14:49.227
I am spending too much time
in front of the computer.


00:14:49.405 --> 00:14:50.872
- Listen to me.
- Aah...


00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.405
We cannot panic.


00:14:52.575 --> 00:14:53.940
We're gonna get through this.


00:14:54.109 --> 00:14:56.077
Okay. Can you let go of my face?


00:14:56.245 --> 00:14:57.269
Will you listen to me?


00:14:57.446 --> 00:14:59.880
Yes, but I really want
you to let go of my face.


00:15:07.022 --> 00:15:09.217
Cut the power to those breakers.


00:15:19.401 --> 00:15:20.732
Good morning, Judy.


00:15:20.903 --> 00:15:22.598
It's pretty grim, huh?


00:15:26.675 --> 00:15:28.939
Well, did Bruce come in already?


00:15:29.478 --> 00:15:31.673
- I don't know.
- Oh.


00:15:31.847 --> 00:15:34.179
- Do you know who Bruce is?
- Yeah.


00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.409
- But you don't know if he walked by?
- No.


00:15:36.785 --> 00:15:38.116
Okay.


00:15:39.154 --> 00:15:41.884
You know, um, we are all hurting.


00:15:42.057 --> 00:15:46.050
And I just wanna say
if there's anything I can do for you...


00:15:46.228 --> 00:15:47.889
Like what?


00:15:48.964 --> 00:15:49.988
I don't know.


00:15:50.165 --> 00:15:52.429
That's why I'm leaving it open-ended.


00:15:52.601 --> 00:15:55.934
You know, sometimes a tragedy
can bring people closer together.


00:15:58.307 --> 00:16:01.834
Or sometimes people prefer to go it alone.


00:16:02.011 --> 00:16:03.740
Like you, probably.


00:16:05.814 --> 00:16:07.611
Okay.


00:16:15.124 --> 00:16:17.388
That wasn't my fault.


00:16:20.029 --> 00:16:23.260
Helena Bonham Carter.
Was there unauthorized revelry in here?


00:16:23.432 --> 00:16:25.423
No, no, no, it was the explosion.


00:16:25.601 --> 00:16:29.935
Shockwave reached all the way down here,
really knocked a lot of stuff loose.


00:16:33.308 --> 00:16:35.469
We're working on a beer-based solvent.


00:16:35.644 --> 00:16:37.703
It's very technical.


00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:40.881
- Where's my invisible blanket?
- You sure it's not on your desk?


00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.711
- It's invisible.
- Think you're funny?


00:16:42.885 --> 00:16:44.648
- Think I don't know what's what?
- What?


00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.153
Chief survived and resumed command.
No one's happier about that than me.


00:16:48.323 --> 00:16:51.315
He's one durable son of a bitch,
but I'm in charge of you, Bruce.


00:16:51.493 --> 00:16:53.256
- I'm Lloyd.
- Do I look stupid to you?


00:16:53.429 --> 00:16:57.229
I promised the chief
the invisibility technology is forthcoming.


00:16:57.399 --> 00:16:58.730
So where the forth is it?


00:16:58.901 --> 00:17:02.132
Oh, it's right here in this cabinet, sir.


00:17:08.277 --> 00:17:12.043
You know what? I just remembered
we still have a bit more work to do on it.


00:17:12.214 --> 00:17:13.442
It's got a torn hem. Um...


00:17:13.615 --> 00:17:16.743
But I assure you, I can have it to you easily
by the end of the day.


00:17:16.919 --> 00:17:19.615
All right, easy.
Stress is the number one cause of herpes.


00:17:19.788 --> 00:17:21.153
Headaches. Which reminds me.


00:17:21.323 --> 00:17:25.259
We have two secret agents, Max and 99,
who will die if they stop being secret.


00:17:25.427 --> 00:17:29.295
Can you imagine how useful it might be
were they to be invisible at this time?


00:17:29.465 --> 00:17:31.365
Got it, life and death, very clear.


00:17:31.533 --> 00:17:33.865
Good. If I have to come
down here one more time...


00:17:34.036 --> 00:17:36.436
...it's gonna be with a bullwhip
and a hockey mask.


00:17:37.005 --> 00:17:38.905
Understood, sir.


00:17:40.008 --> 00:17:41.032
It's not here.


00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:42.234
It's not even here.


00:17:42.411 --> 00:17:43.901
It's missing, it's gone.


00:17:44.079 --> 00:17:45.842
The OCT is MIA.


00:17:46.014 --> 00:17:47.572
- NFW.
- We are dead.


00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.240
- We're not.
- We are.


00:17:49.418 --> 00:17:52.012
You, right now,
are looking at a dead man.


00:17:52.187 --> 00:17:53.916
Whoo.


00:17:54.089 --> 00:17:55.488
Is it hot in here?


00:17:55.657 --> 00:17:58.524
Is it? I must faint now.


00:17:59.561 --> 00:18:00.585
OMG.


00:18:02.064 --> 00:18:03.088
Good, you're back.


00:18:03.265 --> 00:18:07.031
Listen, maybe the OCT is here,
but it's just turned on, so we can't see it.


00:18:07.202 --> 00:18:11.662
- Why wouldn't it be in the cabinet?
- Maybe at the party, someone took it out.


00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.831
To impress another someone.


00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.700
Which it did, by the way.


00:18:17.246 --> 00:18:19.510
- Oh, my God.
- Look, it'll be fine.


00:18:19.681 --> 00:18:23.082
The batteries will wear out,
and it'll be visible in four hours.


00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:26.744
- We're dead.
- I told you.


00:18:26.922 --> 00:18:28.685
The OCT's...


00:18:28.857 --> 00:18:31.985
The OCT is the most
important stealth technology ever created.


00:18:32.161 --> 00:18:34.493
I know. Bruce, come on.


00:18:34.663 --> 00:18:37.791
Listen, the amount
of damage it would do national security...


00:18:37.966 --> 00:18:40.366
...if it fell into the wrong hands
is incalculable.


00:18:40.536 --> 00:18:43.004
- And if KAOS has gotten hold of it...
- Okay, I'm hot.


00:18:43.172 --> 00:18:45.640
- Are you hot right now?
- Do not faint again.


00:18:45.808 --> 00:18:47.070
We can figure this out.


00:18:47.242 --> 00:18:49.005
Who had motive
and who had opportunity?


00:18:49.178 --> 00:18:51.305
Okay, let's just go through the list.


00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:55.314
Who else knew about the OCT
and would benefit from?


00:18:57.019 --> 00:19:00.978
- Bob and Howard.
- Freaking CIA, man.


00:19:06.929 --> 00:19:08.419
Give it.


00:19:09.031 --> 00:19:11.431
- Give what?
- Oh, you know what, don't push me.


00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:15.400
Well, hold up, big man. Be a shame if we
were forced to kick your asses in public.


00:19:15.571 --> 00:19:19.667
No, what would be a shame is if someone
dropped nanorobots in your coffee...


00:19:19.842 --> 00:19:22.777
...got lodged in your colon
and gave you 30 years of diarrhea.


00:19:26.548 --> 00:19:28.812
All right, fine.
Here's your stupid Wiimote.


00:19:28.984 --> 00:19:31.782
- That's not what he's talking about.
- But I'll take that too.


00:19:31.954 --> 00:19:35.685
The Optical Camouflage Technology.
We know you stole it at the party.


00:19:35.858 --> 00:19:38.122
- You wanna go?
- Oh, you got something? Bring it.


00:19:38.293 --> 00:19:39.351
Let's dance.


00:19:39.528 --> 00:19:40.756
I can dance all night.


00:19:40.929 --> 00:19:43.796
Hey, guys, look,
we would never steal from you.


00:19:45.534 --> 00:19:47.058
What are we doing?


00:19:47.236 --> 00:19:49.704
We're all on the same team now.


00:19:49.872 --> 00:19:51.567
What team is that?


00:19:52.174 --> 00:19:53.698
America.


00:19:53.876 --> 00:19:55.537
Perhaps you've heard of it.


00:19:57.179 --> 00:20:00.546
Well, if you hear of anything...


00:20:00.716 --> 00:20:02.445
Of course.


00:20:07.356 --> 00:20:12.157
Hey, can I get a Chicago with extra onions,
extra mustard and extra relish?


00:20:12.327 --> 00:20:14.318
No red pieces,
I don't know what those are.


00:20:14.496 --> 00:20:16.930
How can you eat?
I feel like I'm gonna throw up.


00:20:17.099 --> 00:20:19.533
- There you go.
- Gotta eat past that, man.


00:20:19.701 --> 00:20:22.295
Now I kind of feel guilty
about accusing Bob and Howard.


00:20:22.471 --> 00:20:26.532
Well, they can be jerks,
but deep inside, they're decent guys.


00:20:26.708 --> 00:20:28.073
Those guys are morons.


00:20:28.243 --> 00:20:32.009
All we have to do is recover the OCT
before them, we get all the credit.


00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:34.546
You have no ethics at all, do you, Bob?


00:20:34.716 --> 00:20:36.206
We're the good guys, CIA.


00:20:36.385 --> 00:20:38.819
When we do something,
that makes it ethical.


00:20:48.597 --> 00:20:51.259
- Hey, Nina.
- Hey, is Bruce around?


00:20:51.433 --> 00:20:53.526
No, he went up to Human Resources.


00:20:53.702 --> 00:20:55.966
<i>- At least once an hour ever since.
Can you imagine?</i>


00:20:56.138 --> 00:20:58.106
<i>I don't think the chief ever sleeps.</i>


00:20:59.508 --> 00:21:03.410
Uh, sir, I think you started talking
before you pressed the button.


00:21:03.578 --> 00:21:04.602
Could you repeat that?


00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:05.838
<i>What? I can't hear you.</i>


00:21:06.014 --> 00:21:09.006
<i>But you better have an answer for me,
so get your butts up here.</i>


00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.845
<i>I am a good-looking man.</i>


00:21:14.423 --> 00:21:16.891
<i>I am, I'm a good-looking man.</i>


00:21:17.359 --> 00:21:20.192
<i>- Sir, you need to...
- No question about it.</i>


00:21:20.362 --> 00:21:23.058
You have to, uh, press the button again
to turn it off.


00:21:23.231 --> 00:21:24.630
<i>Goldarn it.</i>


00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.564
Little... Aah.


00:21:31.406 --> 00:21:33.704
I gotta go, the senator's here.


00:21:34.109 --> 00:21:35.474
- Hi.
- Where's Lloyd?


00:21:35.644 --> 00:21:36.872
I'm Lloyd, sir.


00:21:37.045 --> 00:21:38.945
I've worked here for eight years.


00:21:39.314 --> 00:21:43.580
Well, chief asked Bruce to, uh, set up
a satellite scan. I could interrupt them if...


00:21:43.752 --> 00:21:46.414
Why are you still talking there
when I'm here?


00:21:46.588 --> 00:21:48.317
Sorry, sir.


00:21:48.657 --> 00:21:50.921
Watch and tell me
if you notice anything unusual.


00:21:51.093 --> 00:21:54.153
This man is Klaus Kraus,
president of Maraguay.


00:21:54.329 --> 00:21:58.129
A small, angry nation sandwiched
between Paraguay and Uruguay.


00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:01.133
Don't ask why. Huh? Huh?


00:22:02.871 --> 00:22:04.600
Now watch this.


00:22:05.574 --> 00:22:07.974
This was taken
outside the Maraguayan Embassy.


00:22:08.143 --> 00:22:11.010
The man you see here works for Kraus.


00:22:13.548 --> 00:22:16.449
That was my reaction too.
I mean, how can a man just disappear?


00:22:16.618 --> 00:22:19.849
Why, it's almost
as if he had some sort of invisibility cloak.


00:22:20.022 --> 00:22:22.081
We're the only ones
who have that technology.


00:22:22.257 --> 00:22:26.387
Really? If I asked you to produce it
for me this instant, what would you say?


00:22:26.561 --> 00:22:27.789
Well... Huh.


00:22:27.963 --> 00:22:30.363
"Well, huh. " That's what
I thought you'd say.


00:22:30.532 --> 00:22:34.434
We can't have a hostile dictator wandering
around Washington, D.C., invisible.


00:22:34.603 --> 00:22:36.537
He might sell it to KAOS.


00:22:36.705 --> 00:22:37.797
Or France.


00:22:38.807 --> 00:22:40.536
That would be bad, sir.


00:22:40.709 --> 00:22:43.610
Unfortunately, all our agents
are compromised except 99 and 86.


00:22:43.779 --> 00:22:47.442
And they're off in Russia trying
to prevent the annihilation of the world.


00:22:47.616 --> 00:22:50.016
I have to rely on you
and the other pinhead.


00:22:50.185 --> 00:22:52.983
Us? But Bruce and I are just lab guys.


00:22:53.155 --> 00:22:54.179
We're not qualified.


00:22:54.356 --> 00:22:57.723
I'm painfully aware of that,
but I will not have my reputation stained...


00:22:57.893 --> 00:23:00.020
...when I'm this close
to being the big kahuna.


00:23:00.762 --> 00:23:03.458
The president of Maraguay
is leaving the country on Friday.


00:23:03.632 --> 00:23:06.795
You have till Thursday,
that's one day before.


00:23:06.968 --> 00:23:10.870
Get out, come back
and bring me something I can't see.


00:23:11.039 --> 00:23:12.063
I'll try.


00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.299
You'd better.
There's an old Navy expression:


00:23:14.476 --> 00:23:17.570
"If I go down, you go down on me. "


00:23:19.414 --> 00:23:21.279
- You lost me, sir.
- Well, how about this:


00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:22.712
I'll ruin your lives.


00:23:22.884 --> 00:23:24.044
Get out!


00:23:24.786 --> 00:23:26.549
I love when they run. Ha.


00:23:27.923 --> 00:23:29.891
So are you saying that the underchief...


00:23:30.058 --> 00:23:33.494
...is willing to jeopardize national security
just to protect his own ass?


00:23:33.662 --> 00:23:36.062
Yeah, I know it's unheard of
in government, but...


00:23:36.631 --> 00:23:37.825
What are you gonna do?


00:23:37.999 --> 00:23:39.864
- Nice shot.
- Deuce.


00:23:42.337 --> 00:23:45.067
So we can't just walk
into the Maraguayan Embassy and say:


00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:47.868
"Oh, excuse me,
I believe you have something of ours. "


00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:50.740
Problem is, we have no skills.


00:23:50.912 --> 00:23:54.211
Like breaking into buildings,
stealing stuff, shooting people.


00:23:55.951 --> 00:23:57.077
Nice shot.


00:23:58.253 --> 00:24:00.847
Game, set, match, Bruce.


00:24:01.923 --> 00:24:02.981
Wait a minute.


00:24:03.158 --> 00:24:05.388
We don't have to break
into the embassy.


00:24:05.560 --> 00:24:06.857
You're right.


00:24:07.028 --> 00:24:08.188
We could send Neil.


00:24:11.099 --> 00:24:13.465
No, even better.


00:24:19.474 --> 00:24:20.532
Behold.


00:24:21.376 --> 00:24:23.344
- Where's my turtle?
- He's fine.


00:24:23.512 --> 00:24:25.036
He's in the bathroom sink.


00:24:25.213 --> 00:24:26.874
What do you think of Hyme?


00:24:27.048 --> 00:24:28.413
Well, is he fully functional?


00:24:28.583 --> 00:24:31.552
Some of his wiring was damaged
when he was stolen from KAOS.


00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:33.381
So far, he only does this.


00:24:36.324 --> 00:24:38.019
Does he speak?


00:24:39.327 --> 00:24:42.057
If you relax,
your death will be much quicker.


00:24:44.032 --> 00:24:45.499
Okay, almost there.


00:24:46.735 --> 00:24:50.501
Now, before we send Hyme to the embassy,
we need to test his motor skills.


00:24:50.672 --> 00:24:52.367
Rock 'n' roll.


00:24:52.541 --> 00:24:54.805
Okay, this is very simple.


00:24:54.976 --> 00:24:58.309
We're gonna ask you to perform
a series of fine-motor-skill activities.


00:24:58.480 --> 00:25:01.938
The computer will capture movements
and upload them into the robot.


00:25:02.117 --> 00:25:05.109
- Um, I don't wanna do this.
We don't have time to argue.


00:25:05.287 --> 00:25:07.881
Pick up the pencil with your left hand.


00:25:13.128 --> 00:25:14.959
Put down the pencil. Put it down, Neil.


00:25:15.130 --> 00:25:16.495
Put down the pencil, Neil.


00:25:16.665 --> 00:25:17.996
Put it down, put it down.


00:25:22.704 --> 00:25:24.535
Well, he may not be
100 percent ready...


00:25:24.706 --> 00:25:27.106
...but we've got no other choice.


00:25:28.810 --> 00:25:30.675
Okay, we're powered up.


00:25:30.845 --> 00:25:33.143
Send in the Hyme.


00:25:35.083 --> 00:25:36.277
That's what he's called.


00:25:43.058 --> 00:25:44.491
Go left.


00:25:44.659 --> 00:25:45.683
Go left.


00:25:46.094 --> 00:25:48.654
- Left.
- He's not responding.


00:25:50.131 --> 00:25:51.393
Mayday, we got sprinklers.


00:25:51.967 --> 00:25:53.332
Abort, abort.


00:25:53.501 --> 00:25:55.059
Abort, abort.


00:25:55.237 --> 00:25:56.363
Abort.


00:26:02.077 --> 00:26:03.738
Did you reseal the moisture barrier?


00:26:04.112 --> 00:26:05.306
I thought you did.


00:26:05.947 --> 00:26:10.748
Great. First the OCT,
now we lost the Hyme head.


00:26:12.921 --> 00:26:14.013
Found it.


00:26:21.129 --> 00:26:23.029
We're never gonna get Hyme operational.


00:26:23.198 --> 00:26:25.996
We're gonna have to break in,
which we're gonna suck at.


00:26:26.167 --> 00:26:28.567
They're gonna arrest us,
kill us and torture us.


00:26:28.737 --> 00:26:31.535
You're ridiculous.
After they kill us, they can't torture us.


00:26:32.407 --> 00:26:34.898
The worst they could do
is desecrate our bodies.


00:26:35.277 --> 00:26:36.642
We can't do this.


00:26:36.811 --> 00:26:38.039
We're not equipped.


00:26:38.213 --> 00:26:41.376
We're not agents,
we can't go in the field.


00:26:41.549 --> 00:26:43.176
We rarely go out for lunch.


00:26:43.351 --> 00:26:44.375
Stop it.


00:26:44.552 --> 00:26:48.044
We can do this, we're smart people,
I went to MIT.


00:26:48.223 --> 00:26:51.590
You know what? North Dakota Polytechnic
has a very rigorous program.


00:26:51.760 --> 00:26:53.591
There are many roads to the same goal.


00:26:53.762 --> 00:26:54.956
Dude, I wasn't mocking.


00:26:55.430 --> 00:26:57.022
Sounded like you were.


00:26:58.800 --> 00:27:01.360
Oh, God.
Hide the computer, hide everything.


00:27:01.536 --> 00:27:03.766
They're gonna desecrate our bodies.


00:27:04.939 --> 00:27:06.304
- Hi, Nina.
- Hi.


00:27:08.176 --> 00:27:10.542
Hey, Lloyd,
I have good news about the OCT.


00:27:12.747 --> 00:27:16.274
- You told her?
- Did you show him the footage?


00:27:16.584 --> 00:27:18.313
Right.


00:27:19.054 --> 00:27:20.954
Lloyd, remember
the girl in the red dress?


00:27:21.122 --> 00:27:24.558
Vaguely. I mean, there were so many
beautiful girls I spoke to that night.


00:27:24.726 --> 00:27:27.923
Somebody videoed it with a cell phone,
e- mailed it around the office.


00:27:28.096 --> 00:27:29.825
<i>Hello, I'm Isabella.</i>


00:27:29.998 --> 00:27:31.363
<i>Hello, Is...</i>


00:27:31.533 --> 00:27:33.057
<i>Hello, Is...</i>


00:27:33.234 --> 00:27:34.997
<i>Hello, Is...</i>


00:27:35.170 --> 00:27:37.661
I don't normally look at those,
but this was just kind of funny.


00:27:39.240 --> 00:27:41.470
Well, anyways, check this out.


00:27:42.010 --> 00:27:43.910
Don't pay attention
to Karl groping Andrea.


00:27:44.079 --> 00:27:45.979
<i>- Hey.
- Look behind them.</i>


00:27:47.716 --> 00:27:50.150
She's the one that stole the OCT?


00:27:50.318 --> 00:27:52.013
She seemed so nice.


00:27:52.187 --> 00:27:53.415
And lookie, lookie.


00:27:55.223 --> 00:27:57.350
She works for the Maraguayan Embassy?


00:27:57.525 --> 00:27:59.083
She must be our thief.


00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:00.784
You are so smart.


00:28:00.962 --> 00:28:03.055
She went to Caltech, you know.


00:28:23.118 --> 00:28:24.881
- Where is he?
- I don't know.


00:28:25.053 --> 00:28:26.816
Message said for him to meet us here.


00:28:26.988 --> 00:28:28.717
You failed.


00:28:28.890 --> 00:28:32.223
The Maraguayans got to the OCT first.


00:28:32.627 --> 00:28:35.095
Tell me why
I shouldn't kill you right now.


00:28:35.263 --> 00:28:36.924
Well, because we work for you.


00:28:37.098 --> 00:28:39.293
And because it would be murder.


00:28:39.467 --> 00:28:43.335
And our last performance review
was mostly favorable.


00:28:43.505 --> 00:28:45.097
Pipe down. If I wanted you dead...


00:28:45.273 --> 00:28:48.174
...you'd be gurgling that last sentence
through a blood bubble.


00:28:48.343 --> 00:28:51.835
Now, listen, you're gonna get
that invisible blanket into CIA hands...


00:28:52.013 --> 00:28:54.243
...before my brother
at CONTROL can recover it.


00:28:54.416 --> 00:28:58.284
He's been texting me about how he's going
to humiliate me at Thanksgiving this year.


00:28:58.453 --> 00:29:01.479
And let me tell you something,
he does not get to humiliate me.


00:29:01.656 --> 00:29:03.248
I humiliate him.


00:29:03.425 --> 00:29:05.416
That is our relationship.


00:29:05.593 --> 00:29:07.083
- It's understood, sir.
- Shut up.


00:29:08.029 --> 00:29:10.088
You know,
I was born two hours before him.


00:29:10.265 --> 00:29:11.755
Nature wanted me to survive.


00:29:11.933 --> 00:29:15.664
In the lion pride, they kill the runt
of the litter, but not in our family.


00:29:15.837 --> 00:29:17.099
He's so small.


00:29:17.272 --> 00:29:18.899
Better give him the bigger boob.


00:29:21.109 --> 00:29:23.202
Well, who's got the bigger boob now?


00:29:24.512 --> 00:29:27.276
I thought twins were supposed
to have an emotional bond.


00:29:27.449 --> 00:29:29.212
That's a bunch of Hallmark crap.


00:29:29.384 --> 00:29:32.319
Same shoes, matching outfits.


00:29:32.887 --> 00:29:35.378
No kid looks good in a vest.


00:29:35.757 --> 00:29:38.521
- You're right about that, sir.
- Don't suck up, just get it.


00:29:48.636 --> 00:29:50.934
What are you doing?
Reading the CONTROL manual.


00:29:51.105 --> 00:29:53.005
Apparently,
being a spy mostly consists...


00:29:53.174 --> 00:29:55.267
...of sneaking up on people
and shooting them.


00:29:55.443 --> 00:29:58.037
- I'm not comfortable with that.
- There is one thing.


00:29:58.213 --> 00:30:01.649
During World War II, the British
used a technique called the honeytrap.


00:30:01.816 --> 00:30:02.874
I like honey.


00:30:03.051 --> 00:30:06.179
- Not food honey, sexual honey.
- Ew.


00:30:06.354 --> 00:30:09.323
You simply use your manly wiles
and entrap the female target.


00:30:09.491 --> 00:30:10.788
In this case, Isabella.


00:30:11.493 --> 00:30:12.755
Where are your glasses?


00:30:12.927 --> 00:30:14.053
What are you wearing?


00:30:14.229 --> 00:30:15.958
It's Italian. Nina likes it.


00:30:16.130 --> 00:30:17.256
I can see your nipples.


00:30:17.432 --> 00:30:20.094
- No one asked you to look.
- I don't think it's regulation.


00:30:20.268 --> 00:30:22.600
Well, I will change it
if I need to go upstairs.


00:30:23.137 --> 00:30:24.263
- Anyway.
- Anyway.


00:30:24.439 --> 00:30:27.636
Check this. Here are the building
schematics to the Maraguayan Embassy.


00:30:27.809 --> 00:30:31.267
- There's a safe in El Presidente's bedroom.
- That must be where the OCT is.


00:30:31.446 --> 00:30:35.507
Agreed. All I need to do is get a date with
Isabella, use her to get into the embassy...


00:30:35.683 --> 00:30:37.344
...and retrieve the OCT.
- Why you?


00:30:37.519 --> 00:30:39.146
Well, I think that's obvious.


00:30:39.654 --> 00:30:41.815
- I think it isn't.
- I have a girlfriend.


00:30:42.490 --> 00:30:44.720
I choose not to at this time.


00:30:44.893 --> 00:30:47.123
This is too important.
You never speak to women.


00:30:47.295 --> 00:30:48.922
- You have no skills.
- What?


00:30:49.097 --> 00:30:50.223
I have skills.


00:30:50.398 --> 00:30:51.865
I got, like, crazy skills.


00:30:52.033 --> 00:30:54.228
Like, crazy, mad skills, it's insane...


00:30:54.402 --> 00:30:56.529
Fine, you really think you can do this?


00:30:56.704 --> 00:30:57.830
I know I can.


00:30:58.606 --> 00:31:00.096
All right. Go, player.


00:31:00.275 --> 00:31:01.867
Rock it.


00:31:09.551 --> 00:31:11.212
- Hey, Judy.
- Don't lean on my desk.


00:31:13.021 --> 00:31:14.113
Uh...


00:31:14.289 --> 00:31:16.348
What you doing there?
Is that a crossword?


00:31:16.524 --> 00:31:19.857
- So?
- So nothing.


00:31:20.028 --> 00:31:21.461
I just...


00:31:21.629 --> 00:31:25.929
I also like crosswords. Huh.


00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:31.333
Wow, I didn't really know
that we had that much in common.


00:31:32.707 --> 00:31:35.232
Actually, it's pretty crazy. Hm-hm.


00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:36.468
Are you hitting on me?


00:31:37.211 --> 00:31:39.577
No. Wow, no, no, not at all.


00:31:39.747 --> 00:31:41.339
I just...


00:31:41.516 --> 00:31:46.078
Okay, actually, I was practicing
hitting on someone on you.


00:31:46.621 --> 00:31:50.057
Look, I know we really don't talk a lot,
but I've been assigned this case.


00:31:50.224 --> 00:31:54.354
And there's this female suspect,
but I don't go out a lot.


00:31:54.529 --> 00:31:57.430
Well, I go outside, outdoors. Ha-ha.


00:31:57.599 --> 00:32:00.033
But I just don't go out.


00:32:00.201 --> 00:32:01.896
With women. I want to.


00:32:02.070 --> 00:32:03.332
Obviously, I want to.


00:32:03.504 --> 00:32:05.199
Yes, I want to, but...


00:32:06.908 --> 00:32:10.071
Not because there's a lack of interest.
It's not lack of anything. Ha.


00:32:10.244 --> 00:32:12.178
If you know what I mean.


00:32:13.181 --> 00:32:14.876
I'm just dedicated to my work.


00:32:15.049 --> 00:32:17.609
I think that's pretty admirable.


00:32:18.987 --> 00:32:20.784
Will you please help me?


00:32:22.290 --> 00:32:25.054
- Give her flowers.
- That's it?


00:32:25.226 --> 00:32:26.523
And don't talk.


00:32:27.428 --> 00:32:28.952
Even when I give her the flowers?


00:32:29.130 --> 00:32:32.861
Because I think if I don't say anything,
it might get a little awkward. Ha-ha.


00:32:33.368 --> 00:32:34.460
I mean, to me.


00:32:34.969 --> 00:32:36.869
Oh.


00:32:37.271 --> 00:32:38.295
Got it.


00:32:38.473 --> 00:32:40.941
Well, thank you for your help.


00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:43.800
I'll go.


00:33:25.253 --> 00:33:27.778
- What?
- Why haven't you talked to her yet?


00:33:27.955 --> 00:33:30.480
<i>- How do you know I haven't?
- Because I'm watching you.</i>


00:33:30.658 --> 00:33:33.855
The street cameras. Hello?
What is taking you so long?


00:33:34.028 --> 00:33:37.987
Maraguayan president's leaving in two days.
We have to get the OCT back before then.


00:33:38.166 --> 00:33:39.531
Now, man up.


00:33:39.701 --> 00:33:42.602
I'd have confidence if I was wearing
one of your nipple shirts.


00:33:42.770 --> 00:33:44.499
I'm hanging up now.


00:33:45.139 --> 00:33:47.232
Hi, Isabella. Isabella, is that you?


00:33:47.408 --> 00:33:48.670
Remember me?


00:33:48.843 --> 00:33:49.867
May I help you, sir?


00:33:50.378 --> 00:33:53.370
- Uh, it's okay, I'm meeting someone.
- Not in here.


00:33:53.981 --> 00:33:55.710
- Excuse me?
- We have a dress code.


00:33:55.883 --> 00:33:57.544
You're not wearing socks.


00:33:59.420 --> 00:34:00.944
Come on.


00:34:01.122 --> 00:34:03.022
I mean, a lot of people don't wear socks.


00:34:03.191 --> 00:34:05.284
I can see four women
in sandals and no socks.


00:34:05.460 --> 00:34:07.291
Do you see any men with no socks?


00:34:07.462 --> 00:34:10.226
- I don't know, I didn't check them all.
- Well, I have.


00:34:10.398 --> 00:34:12.832
I'm not gonna go all the way home
and put on socks...


00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.730
...just so I can sit
in your snooty restaurant.


00:34:17.371 --> 00:34:18.736
Come on, this is retarded.


00:34:18.906 --> 00:34:20.703
My cousin is retarded.


00:34:22.543 --> 00:34:24.135
I'm sorry.


00:34:24.412 --> 00:34:26.505
I'll be right back.


00:34:27.048 --> 00:34:28.709
- Hold up there, big man.
- Bob?


00:34:28.883 --> 00:34:30.373
- Yeah.
- What are you doing here?


00:34:30.985 --> 00:34:34.512
How about you and I go down the street,
and I'll buy you a couple of pizzas?


00:34:34.689 --> 00:34:36.589
Right, you're just a lab rat like me.


00:34:36.758 --> 00:34:39.625
You really think I'm gonna believe
you have a gun under there?


00:34:39.794 --> 00:34:42.058
- Oh, jeez.
- Excuse me, gentlemen.


00:34:44.999 --> 00:34:48.264
Isabella, right? Howard.
I met you at the party the other night.


00:34:48.770 --> 00:34:50.067
Mike, thanks again.


00:34:50.238 --> 00:34:52.763
My pleasure, Bob.
Are we still on for Cirque du Soleil?


00:34:54.742 --> 00:34:57.302
Come here.
A little out of your league, aren't you?


00:34:57.478 --> 00:34:59.969
Why don't you let the agency
handle it from here?


00:35:00.148 --> 00:35:01.206
Please, sit down.


00:35:02.517 --> 00:35:05.509
You let them get to Isabella first?
Are you crazy?


00:35:06.354 --> 00:35:09.118
I should have done it myself.
You have no skills.


00:35:09.657 --> 00:35:12.524
Oh, okay. Look who's suddenly
God's gift to women.


00:35:12.693 --> 00:35:15.753
- Well, I'm the one with the girlfriend.
- You mean Yoko?


00:35:15.930 --> 00:35:18.956
I find that offensive on so many levels.


00:35:19.534 --> 00:35:22.094
You wouldn't even have a girlfriend
if it wasn't for me.


00:35:22.270 --> 00:35:25.137
Excuse me, I don't remember
a really fat Cupid flying over me.


00:35:25.306 --> 00:35:26.773
I'm talking about her smell.


00:35:26.941 --> 00:35:29.136
The only reason
you can tolerate her presence...


00:35:29.310 --> 00:35:33.041
...is because I invented a pheromone
that neutralizes the formaldehyde emissions.


00:35:33.214 --> 00:35:34.875
- That's a lie.
- It's the truth.


00:35:35.049 --> 00:35:38.416
It's an anti-smell tailored specifically
to Nina's repulsive odor.


00:35:38.586 --> 00:35:41.646
Like noise-canceling headphones,
but for Nina's unique stank.


00:35:41.823 --> 00:35:43.950
I've been misting her
twice a day secretly.


00:35:53.167 --> 00:35:54.498
Not anymore.


00:35:55.436 --> 00:35:57.768
I don't care.
We don't need your stupid spray.


00:35:57.939 --> 00:35:59.804
Oh, yeah?
Why don't you call me around 9?


00:35:59.974 --> 00:36:01.737
Let me know how that's going.


00:36:21.193 --> 00:36:22.922
I'm what?


00:36:23.296 --> 00:36:26.231
Oh, come on, Nina. Please don't leave.


00:36:26.399 --> 00:36:28.424
I didn't say it was a bad smell.


00:36:28.601 --> 00:36:32.731
It's unique, distinctive, idiosyncratic.


00:36:32.905 --> 00:36:38.036
For future reference,
the word "putrid" is a real mood killer.


00:37:15.414 --> 00:37:17.041
Dude.


00:37:17.516 --> 00:37:19.643
You're killing me, seriously.


00:37:24.724 --> 00:37:26.624
Thank you.


00:37:47.613 --> 00:37:48.773
You wanted to see me?


00:37:52.184 --> 00:37:54.584
Always. You've done well.


00:37:54.754 --> 00:37:58.850
KAOS has offered to pay $50 million
for the invisible fabric...


00:37:59.025 --> 00:38:02.085
...which, as you know,
is double our gross national product.


00:38:02.628 --> 00:38:06.064
But now, I think these scientists
who created it...


00:38:06.232 --> 00:38:07.563
...are worth even more to me.


00:38:07.733 --> 00:38:09.826
So I need you to bring them here.


00:38:10.002 --> 00:38:13.631
But you already have a weapons expert
working for you.


00:38:13.806 --> 00:38:15.637
Oh, he is useless.


00:38:15.808 --> 00:38:18.470
I give him this spacious prison cell.


00:38:18.644 --> 00:38:20.111
I give him some food.


00:38:20.279 --> 00:38:22.679
And in 15 years,
he gives me nothing of value...


00:38:22.848 --> 00:38:25.976
...except some sort of engine
that runs on water.


00:38:26.152 --> 00:38:28.552
Hello? That's what gasoline is for.


00:38:29.155 --> 00:38:31.453
So you will release him.


00:38:31.624 --> 00:38:33.148
No, I will shoot him.


00:38:33.325 --> 00:38:35.350
Or someone who works for me
will shoot him.


00:38:35.528 --> 00:38:38.497
Either way, there will be a shooting.


00:38:51.977 --> 00:38:54.775
Guys, are we gonna work today
or are you just gonna stand...


00:38:54.947 --> 00:38:56.676
...in stony silence, like my parents?


00:38:57.183 --> 00:38:59.014
Well, Neil, I'm here ready to work...


00:38:59.185 --> 00:39:02.245
...whereas Lloyd showed up looking
like yesterday's cottage cheese.


00:39:02.421 --> 00:39:04.286
Perhaps you should ask him.


00:39:04.457 --> 00:39:06.584
Perhaps you can tell Bruce
that I'm sorry...


00:39:06.759 --> 00:39:08.920
...my grooming does not meet
with his approval.


00:39:09.095 --> 00:39:10.460
Neil, please tell Lloyd:


00:39:12.098 --> 00:39:13.725
Neil, please tell Bruce:


00:39:20.940 --> 00:39:22.305
Oh, hey, Nina.


00:39:22.475 --> 00:39:25.933
Look, I know that you and Bruce
have been friends for a really long time...


00:39:26.112 --> 00:39:29.377
