that I'm being Yoko.


00:39:29.548 --> 00:39:31.846
Hey. No, no one thinks that.


00:39:32.017 --> 00:39:33.678
Ugh. Oh, what is that?


00:39:33.853 --> 00:39:38.256
That smells like a dead cat
covered in old shrimp. Is that me?


00:39:38.424 --> 00:39:41.757
Yeah. Apparently, um,
I reek with the stench of death.


00:39:41.927 --> 00:39:44.088
- Oh.
- Yeah, I'm putrid.


00:39:44.263 --> 00:39:46.788
But I'm actually so grateful
that he told me, you know?


00:39:46.966 --> 00:39:49.230
Ever since I got
into forensics in grad school...


00:39:49.401 --> 00:39:53.337
...I noticed that people were drifting away
from me, like far, far, away.


00:39:53.506 --> 00:39:56.407
I thought it was because
I was weird or hard to get along with.


00:39:56.575 --> 00:39:58.042
You're not. You're nice.


00:39:58.210 --> 00:39:59.404
- Well, thank you.
- Whoa.


00:39:59.979 --> 00:40:02.743
I think a monkey died
in the air vent again.


00:40:02.915 --> 00:40:04.906
So this is actually a huge relief,
you know?


00:40:05.084 --> 00:40:09.111
I can look at myself in the mirror and say,
"Hey, I do not have a personality defect.


00:40:09.288 --> 00:40:11.119
I just smell like rotting flesh. "


00:40:11.290 --> 00:40:12.314
That must feel great.


00:40:12.491 --> 00:40:14.152
- Yeah.
- Oh, God, what is that?


00:40:14.326 --> 00:40:16.624
Smells like pig vomit. Pig vomit.


00:40:16.796 --> 00:40:20.527
Hey, look. Remember Howard? The one
that snaked you with the Maraguayan girl?


00:40:21.033 --> 00:40:22.762
<i>Message said for him to meet us here.</i>


00:40:22.935 --> 00:40:25.426
We received our own
surveillance footage from Langley.


00:40:25.871 --> 00:40:27.065
<i>Listen.</i>


00:40:27.239 --> 00:40:28.399
Look at them.


00:40:28.574 --> 00:40:32.601
<i>We'll find a way to get
that invisible blanket into CIA hands.</i>


00:40:32.778 --> 00:40:34.871
Bob and Howard know
Isabella has the OCT...


00:40:35.047 --> 00:40:37.038
...and are meeting
at the restaurant tonight.


00:40:37.216 --> 00:40:38.911
We have to get there before they do.


00:40:39.084 --> 00:40:40.608
Good afternoon, Nina.


00:40:41.954 --> 00:40:43.478
Bruce.


00:40:43.656 --> 00:40:46.124
I see you're wearing the sunglasses
that I bought you.


00:40:46.292 --> 00:40:49.420
Yes. I had a bad night,
so I finished off that bottle of tequila.


00:40:50.229 --> 00:40:51.856
So did you figure something out?


00:40:52.031 --> 00:40:56.024
Well, just that Bob and Howard
are going after the OCT tonight.


00:40:59.805 --> 00:41:02.865
Did you hear me or are we still
being childish and not talking?


00:41:03.042 --> 00:41:04.566
I can see the OCT.


00:41:04.743 --> 00:41:06.142
That's impossible.


00:41:06.312 --> 00:41:07.336
Not the whole thing.


00:41:07.513 --> 00:41:09.981
Just a tiny test scrap we had left over.


00:41:10.149 --> 00:41:12.049
I can see it. Wait.


00:41:16.789 --> 00:41:20.156
- It's my glasses.
- You invented anti-OCT sunglasses?


00:41:20.326 --> 00:41:22.294
No, I didn't invent them. They're Oakleys.


00:41:22.461 --> 00:41:24.986
Are you telling me
a multi-billion-dollar technology...


00:41:25.164 --> 00:41:28.656
...for altering the laws of physics
can be defeated by cheap sunglasses?


00:41:28.834 --> 00:41:30.893
They're not cheap. They're Oakleys.


00:41:31.403 --> 00:41:32.427
They're polarized.


00:41:32.605 --> 00:41:36.200
I remember because the salesman
told me they're polarized.


00:41:36.542 --> 00:41:37.907
I think he was hitting on me.


00:41:38.811 --> 00:41:39.937
Well.


00:41:54.159 --> 00:41:55.854
Okay. There's Isabella.


00:41:56.028 --> 00:41:58.519
Howard should be here any minute.


00:41:59.298 --> 00:42:01.994
So, Bruce,
notice anything different about Nina?


00:42:05.437 --> 00:42:07.632
Your smell, which you don't have.


00:42:07.806 --> 00:42:11.003
- Why don't you have it?
- Say thank you to Lloyd.


00:42:11.510 --> 00:42:12.704
She shouldn't be punished.


00:42:12.878 --> 00:42:14.812
You're the one being a dick.


00:42:16.015 --> 00:42:18.245
Oh, here he comes.


00:42:20.853 --> 00:42:23.321
Look at that little rat
trying to steal our invention.


00:42:23.489 --> 00:42:24.547
Thank you.


00:42:25.224 --> 00:42:28.159
He wants to act like a rodent,
we'll treat him like one.


00:42:29.728 --> 00:42:31.559
Powering up.


00:42:31.730 --> 00:42:33.391
- Hey.
- Whoa.


00:42:46.545 --> 00:42:47.944
What's the matter?


00:42:50.416 --> 00:42:52.179
My hair.


00:42:54.420 --> 00:42:55.444
I'll be right back.


00:42:55.621 --> 00:42:56.918
I'll...


00:43:02.594 --> 00:43:04.118
Go.


00:43:05.364 --> 00:43:08.197
Hey, Isabella, right?


00:43:09.835 --> 00:43:11.735
Yeah, I'm Lloyd.


00:43:11.904 --> 00:43:14.600
Didn't we meet at my party
the other night?


00:43:14.773 --> 00:43:17.537
I'm here with my friend, Bruce,
and his girlfriend, Nina.


00:43:17.710 --> 00:43:19.200
And...


00:43:21.780 --> 00:43:24.840
Would you want to join us? Come on.


00:43:25.484 --> 00:43:27.111
- I got you flowers and everything.
- Ha.


00:43:29.321 --> 00:43:33.451
Well, maybe I could have
just one glass of wine.


00:43:33.625 --> 00:43:34.887
Ha.


00:43:35.060 --> 00:43:38.427
Great.
I'll just have the waiter add another chair.


00:43:46.038 --> 00:43:47.733
She said yes?


00:43:48.040 --> 00:43:49.234
I gave her flowers.


00:43:49.408 --> 00:43:50.739
The chicks dig it.


00:43:50.909 --> 00:43:53.002
Just, uh, FYI.


00:43:53.512 --> 00:43:56.242
Four, two, one, one, seven...


00:43:56.415 --> 00:43:58.883
<i>...zero, six, seven, nine.
Zero, six, seven, nine.</i>


00:43:59.051 --> 00:44:00.712
Pi to 100 places.


00:44:00.886 --> 00:44:03.878
North Dakota Polytechnic
must be a very fine school.


00:44:09.561 --> 00:44:11.927
I have to go to the bathroom.


00:44:14.533 --> 00:44:16.296
I just love her accent.


00:44:16.468 --> 00:44:18.333
Waitress, can we have another bottle?


00:44:18.504 --> 00:44:20.131
Certainly, sir.


00:44:20.305 --> 00:44:21.897
How are we not drunk too?


00:44:23.742 --> 00:44:24.766
ANS.


00:44:24.943 --> 00:44:26.877
Alcohol Neutralization Solution.


00:44:27.046 --> 00:44:29.571
One drop,
you might as well be drinking lemonade.


00:44:29.748 --> 00:44:32.581
Oh, my gosh. You could make
so much money off of that.


00:44:32.751 --> 00:44:35.447
We don't do it for the money.
We do this for our country.


00:44:36.388 --> 00:44:37.582
Oh, I have to warn you.


00:44:37.756 --> 00:44:39.417
Your pee will be blue later.


00:44:39.591 --> 00:44:41.525
It's harmless, but it can be alarming.


00:44:43.362 --> 00:44:44.488
I have them.


00:44:45.964 --> 00:44:47.431
But I want to make a deal.


00:44:47.966 --> 00:44:49.831
You what?


00:44:50.369 --> 00:44:52.929
I don't make deals with my employees.


00:44:53.105 --> 00:44:54.436
I have something you want.


00:44:54.606 --> 00:44:55.971
I want something too.


00:44:56.141 --> 00:44:59.304
I will trade you the Americans
for the scientist you already have.


00:45:02.481 --> 00:45:06.042
You realize you can never return
to Maraguay now, hmm?


00:45:06.218 --> 00:45:09.710
The deforested plains, the, uh,
third-highest-quality cocaine...


00:45:09.888 --> 00:45:11.549
...in all of South America.


00:45:11.723 --> 00:45:13.714
Vast fields of old tires.


00:45:13.892 --> 00:45:16.827
Yes, I will miss its splendor.


00:45:16.995 --> 00:45:18.963
Take it or leave it.


00:45:20.466 --> 00:45:23.060
It appears I have no choice.


00:45:27.272 --> 00:45:29.137
When she gets here, kill her.


00:45:29.308 --> 00:45:31.742
<i>I'm watching Iron Chef and going to bed.</i>


00:45:33.479 --> 00:45:35.879
Now all we have to do
is get her to invite us...


00:45:36.048 --> 00:45:37.572
...to her embassy for a nightcap.


00:45:37.749 --> 00:45:40.013
Like that's ever gonna happen.


00:45:40.752 --> 00:45:42.310
I have a great idea.


00:45:48.794 --> 00:45:50.284
Shh. Shh.


00:45:59.771 --> 00:46:01.762
- Dude.
- I know.


00:46:01.940 --> 00:46:03.430
Shh.


00:46:04.109 --> 00:46:05.474
Let's go to the kitchen.


00:46:05.644 --> 00:46:07.111
There is wine there.


00:46:07.279 --> 00:46:08.746
Wait.


00:46:08.914 --> 00:46:10.347
Now I have to go the bathroom.


00:46:10.516 --> 00:46:11.813
I will show you where it is.


00:46:11.984 --> 00:46:13.747
You, wait here.


00:46:13.919 --> 00:46:15.216
You are cute. Ha-ha.


00:46:15.387 --> 00:46:17.287
They are cute.


00:46:22.094 --> 00:46:25.291
- You know, I think Lloyd really likes you.
- Ha-ha.


00:46:25.464 --> 00:46:26.488
I know.


00:46:26.665 --> 00:46:29.691
It's funny. I've never dated a Asian man.


00:46:29.868 --> 00:46:31.495
No, that's Bruce.


00:46:31.670 --> 00:46:32.694
Oh, right.


00:46:33.372 --> 00:46:35.067
Well, this is going well.


00:46:35.240 --> 00:46:36.730
Yeah.


00:46:38.143 --> 00:46:41.044
- Why are you saying it like that?
- Well, it's just surprising.


00:46:41.213 --> 00:46:45.445
I mean, Isabella seemed
to fall for you rather easily.


00:46:45.617 --> 00:46:47.050
Well, I'm kind of charming.


00:46:47.219 --> 00:46:49.084
And three bottles of wine.


